## Plan

_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/39684677739)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

`cargo jackioh fuzz --duos` plays each seed under a co-op match's setup, rotating by seed the way `handicap_for_seed` does: team B (the AI team) at Easy, Medium or Hard with `duos_ai_team(tier)` rules and `AI_DIFFICULTY[tier]` on B1 and B2, decks sized to those handicaps, and none, one or two seats' decks dealt (R433). Done means: a unit test pins the rotation and shows two seeds create different options; one rotation deals a seat in each duel and on team B, and a test reads `create_duel`'s filter result off both duels; a failure's report (text and `--json`) names the seed's setup and options next to the seed and all four decks.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `crates/tools/src/duos_fuzz.rs` | change | header doc; imports; `DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS`, `DUOS_DEALT_SEATS`, `DuosSetup`, `duos_setup_for_seed`, `duos_decks_for_handicaps`, `duos_options_for_seed`, `failure_report`, `setup_options_json`; `duos_decks_for_seed` made `#[cfg(test)]`; `play_duos_game_inner`, `failure_lines` and `wave_json` use them; five new tests |
| `crates/tools/README.md` | change | the `fuzz` row's `--duos` text: one sentence on the rotation and the failure report |

Do not touch: `crates/engine/`, `crates/ai/`, `crates/server/`, `crates/cards/`, `crates/tools/src/fuzz.rs`, `crates/tools/src/replay.rs`, `spec/`, `.github/`. No ruling: §13.7's tier table and the server's `crates/server/src/duos/engine.rs::dealt_options` (which this mirrors) settle every rule. The governing text is SPEC §13.7, §9.9, R184 and R433.

## Steps

1. **`crates/tools/src/duos_fuzz.rs`, the module header.** Replace the first sentence of the paragraph at lines 18–20 (from `//! A seed fixes the game:` up to `why that is what replay equality proves).`) with the text below. Keep the sentence after it (`The policy is §10.7's over a …`) as it is.
   ```rust
   //! A seed fixes the game. Its setup rotates by seed the way a co-op match is made (§13.7, #1573,
   //! `duos_setup_for_seed`): team A plays `DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM` with no handicap, team B is the AI team at
   //! one of `DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS`, under `duos_ai_team` with `AI_DIFFICULTY`'s handicap on each seat (none at
   //! Easy), and the seats of one of `DUOS_DEALT_SEATS` play a dealt deck (R433). The four decks are one
   //! seeded shuffle of the gate's pool (`FUZZ_POOL`), dealt in seat order at each seat's deck size
   //! (R184), so no card is in two decks, and a failure prints the setup, the options and every deck.
   //! The policy's picks come from streams of the seed's own, outside the state (`fuzz.rs`'s header
   //! says why that is what replay equality proves).
   ```

2. **Imports.** In the `use jackioh_engine::{ … };` block (lines 35–41), add `AI_DIFFICULTY`, `DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM`, `Difficulty`, `DuosHandicaps`, `HUMAN_HANDICAP`, `PerTeam` and `duos_ai_team` (all re-exported at the engine's root). Run `cargo fmt -p jackioh-tools` at the end to sort them.

3. **`duos_decks_for_seed` (line 104).** Put `#[cfg(test)]` above it and make its body `duos_decks_for_handicaps(seed, &DuosHandicaps::default())`. Keep its doc comment and append this line to it:
   ```rust
   /// `duos_decks_for_handicaps` with no handicap: the decks `cargo test`'s co-op games deal.
   ```
   This keeps every seed's deal unchanged when no handicap applies. Without the attribute it becomes dead code in the binary once step 5 lands, and clippy fails on that. Its only other caller is `replay.rs`'s `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`.

4. **New items, right after `duos_decks_for_seed`.** Add exactly:
   ```rust
   /// The tiers the seeds rotate the AI team (team B) through (#1573), as a co-op match sets it up
   /// (§13.7): its rules `duos_ai_team(tier)` and each of its seats' handicap `AI_DIFFICULTY[tier]`.
   /// Easy is the humans' rules and resources, the setup every seed played before #1573.
   const DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS: [Difficulty; 3] = [Difficulty::Easy, Difficulty::Medium, Difficulty::Hard];

   /// The seats whose deck a seed deals rather than builds (R433), rotating (#1573): none; A1's alone,
   /// so duel 1 deals none; A2's and B1's, a seat of each duel and of each team, so `create_duel` maps a
   /// team B seat to its duel's `p2`; both human seats', as a match of two All Random players has it.
   const DUOS_DEALT_SEATS: [&[DuosSeat]; 4] = [
       &[],
       &[DuosSeat::A1],
       &[DuosSeat::A2, DuosSeat::B1],
       &[DuosSeat::A1, DuosSeat::A2],
   ];

   /// One seed's setup beyond its decks (#1573): the AI team's tier and the seats dealt their deck.
   /// Team A always plays `DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM` with no handicap, as a co-op match's people do (§13.7).
   #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
   struct DuosSetup {
       tier: Difficulty,
       dealt: &'static [DuosSeat],
   }

   impl DuosSetup {
       /// Each seat's handicap: team B's `AI_DIFFICULTY[tier]`, none at Easy, whose resources are a
       /// person's (a co-op match stores none for it either); team A's none.
       fn handicaps(self) -> DuosHandicaps {
           let handicap = AI_DIFFICULTY[self.tier];
           let ai = (handicap != HUMAN_HANDICAP).then_some(handicap);
           DuosHandicaps {
               a1: None,
               a2: None,
               b1: ai,
               b2: ai,
           }
       }

       /// What a failure prints for the setup: `AI team <tier>, dealt <seats, or none>`.
       fn label(self) -> String {
           let dealt: Vec<&str> = self.dealt.iter().map(|seat| seat.as_str()).collect();
           let dealt = if dealt.is_empty() {
               "none".to_string()
           } else {
               dealt.join(", ")
           };
           format!("AI team {}, dealt {dealt}", self.tier)
       }
   }

   /// The seed's setup (#1573), rotating as `handicap_for_seed` does: the tier by the seed modulo the
   /// tiers, the dealt seats by the quotient, so every 12 consecutive seeds play each pairing once. The
   /// seed alone fixes it, so `--from <seed> --seeds 1` plays the same game.
   fn duos_setup_for_seed(seed: u32) -> DuosSetup {
       let at = usize::try_from(seed).unwrap_or(0);
       let tiers = DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS.len();
       DuosSetup {
           tier: DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS[at % tiers],
           dealt: DUOS_DEALT_SEATS[(at / tiers) % DUOS_DEALT_SEATS.len()],
       }
   }

   /// One seeded shuffle of the pool dealt in seat order (A1, A2, B1, B2), each seat its handicap's
   /// deck size (R184) or DECK_SIZE, so no card is in two decks. Team A's two decks, and with no
   /// handicap all four, are the ones every seed was dealt before #1573.
   fn duos_decks_for_handicaps(seed: u32, handicaps: &DuosHandicaps) -> DuosDecks {
       let mut rng = Rng::new(&format!("jackioh-duos-fuzz-decks-{seed}"), 0);
       let mut rest = rng.shuffle(FUZZ_POOL.as_slice()).into_iter();
       let mut deal = |seat: DuosSeat| -> Vec<String> {
           let size = handicaps.get(seat).map_or(DECK_SIZE, |handicap| handicap.deck_size);
           rest.by_ref().take(usize::try_from(size).unwrap_or(0)).collect()
       };
       DuosDecks {
           a1: deal(DuosSeat::A1),
           a2: deal(DuosSeat::A2),
           b1: deal(DuosSeat::B1),
           b2: deal(DuosSeat::B2),
       }
   }

   /// What seed `seed`'s game is created, folded and checkpointed with (#1573): its stream, its setup's
   /// team rules, handicaps and dealt seats, and decks sized to the handicaps.
   fn duos_options_for_seed(seed: u32) -> DuosCreateOptions {
       let setup = duos_setup_for_seed(seed);
       let handicaps = setup.handicaps();
       DuosCreateOptions {
           seed: format!("jackioh-duos-fuzz-{seed}"),
           decks: duos_decks_for_handicaps(seed, &handicaps),
           teams: Some(PerTeam::new(DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM, duos_ai_team(setup.tier))),
           handicaps: Some(handicaps),
           dealt: (!setup.dealt.is_empty()).then(|| setup.dealt.to_vec()),
           ..DuosCreateOptions::default()
       }
   }
   ```

5. **`play_duos_game_inner` (line 260).** Replace the `let options = DuosCreateOptions { seed: …, decks: duos_decks_for_seed(seed), ..DuosCreateOptions::default() };` statement with `let options = duos_options_for_seed(seed);`. Change nothing else there. The fold (`check_duos_run`) and the checkpoint already read `run.options`.

6. **`failure_lines` (line 603).** Change its `.map(|error| format!("seed {}: {error}", outcome.seed))` to `.map(|error| failure_report(outcome.seed, error))`. Each entry stays one string, so `run`'s count and the tests' `lines.len()` are unchanged. Add right after `failure_lines`:
   ```rust
   /// One failed seed's report (#1573): `seed N: <error>`, then what its game was created with, the
   /// setup, the options a fold takes besides the seed and decks, and each seat's deck, as the 1v1
   /// report prints its two.
   fn failure_report(seed: u32, error: &str) -> String {
       let options = duos_options_for_seed(seed);
       let mut lines = vec![
           format!("seed {seed}: {error}"),
           format!("  setup: {}", duos_setup_for_seed(seed).label()),
           format!("  options: {}", setup_options_json(&options)),
       ];
       for seat in DUOS_SEATS {
           lines.push(format!("  seed {seed} {seat} deck: {}", options.decks.of(seat).join(", ")));
       }
       lines.join("\n")
   }

   /// The options a seed's game was created with besides its seed and decks (#1573): the teams'
   /// rules, the seats' handicaps and the dealt seats, as one JSON object.
   fn setup_options_json(options: &DuosCreateOptions) -> serde_json::Value {
       serde_json::json!({
           "teams": options.teams,
           "handicaps": options.handicaps,
           "dealt": options.dealt,
       })
   }
   ```

7. **`wave_json` (line 652).** In the failure object `serde_json::json!({ "seed": outcome.seed, "message": error, })`, add `"options": duos_options_for_seed(outcome.seed),` after `"message"`. In its doc comment, change `Failures carry only seed and message:` to `Failures carry the seed, the message and the seed's whole create options (#1573):`.

8. **Tests.** Add the five tests below (see **Tests**) to `mod tests` in the same file, after `the_four_decks_come_from_the_seed_alone_and_share_no_card`. Leave every existing test unchanged.

9. **`crates/tools/README.md`, line 15, the `fuzz` row.** Right after this text:
   ```
   `duos_fold`ed back to its live `duos_hash`; 200 seeds by default.
   ```
   insert a space and then this, on the same line. Change nothing else.
   ```
   Each seed plays a co-op match's setup, rotating by seed (#1573): the AI team (team B) at Easy, Medium or Hard, under `duos_ai_team(tier)` with `AI_DIFFICULTY[tier]`'s handicap on each of its seats (none at Easy), each deck dealt at its seat's deck size, and none, one or two seats' decks dealt (R433), so `--from` replays it; a failure prints the seed's setup, the options a fold takes besides the decks and all four decks, and `--duos --json` gives each failure the seed's whole `DuosCreateOptions`.
   ```

10. Run `cargo fmt -p jackioh-tools`, then the commands under **Tests** and **Done when**.

## Tests

All in `crates/tools/src/duos_fuzz.rs`, `mod tests`:

- `the_setup_rotates_by_seed_through_every_tier_and_dealt_seats`: `duos_setup_for_seed(1) == DuosSetup { tier: Difficulty::Medium, dealt: &[] }`, `(2)` Hard with `&[]`, `(3)` Easy with `&[DuosSeat::A1]`, `(7)` Medium with `&[DuosSeat::A2, DuosSeat::B1]` and `(11)` Hard with `&[DuosSeat::A1, DuosSeat::A2]`. Then `let seen: Vec<DuosSetup> = (1..=12).map(duos_setup_for_seed).collect();` and, `for tier in DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS { for dealt in DUOS_DEALT_SEATS { … } }`, assert `seen.contains(&DuosSetup { tier, dealt })` with message `"{tier} {dealt:?}"`.
- `two_seeds_create_different_options_and_a_seed_always_the_same`: `assert_eq!(duos_options_for_seed(7), duos_options_for_seed(7))`; with `medium = duos_options_for_seed(1)` and `hard = duos_options_for_seed(2)`, `assert_ne!` on `.teams` and on `.handicaps`; `assert_ne!(duos_options_for_seed(1).dealt, duos_options_for_seed(4).dealt)` (seed 4 deals A1).
- `a_seed_s_options_are_a_co_op_match_s_at_its_tier`: for `seed in 1..=3`, with `tier = duos_setup_for_seed(seed).tier` and `options = duos_options_for_seed(seed)`, check four things. First, `options.teams == Some(PerTeam::new(DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM, duos_ai_team(tier)))`. Second, with `handicaps = options.handicaps.clone().expect(…)`, `(handicaps.a1, handicaps.a2) == (None, None)` and `(handicaps.b1, handicaps.b2) == (ai, ai)` where `ai = (tier != Difficulty::Easy).then_some(AI_DIFFICULTY[tier])`. Third, for each seat of `DUOS_SEATS`, `options.decks.of(seat).len()` equals `usize::try_from(handicaps.get(seat).map_or(DECK_SIZE, |h| h.deck_size)).unwrap_or(0)`, and an `indexmap::IndexSet` of all four decks' ids is as long as their total (no card twice). Fourth, `options.decks.a1`/`a2` equal `duos_decks_for_seed(seed).a1`/`a2`.
- `a_dealt_seat_is_dealt_in_its_own_duel_and_seat_only` (covers `create_duel`'s filter): `use jackioh_engine::PlayerId;`, call `register_all();` and `let _preview = preview_every_set();`, then a closure `dealt(seed)` that maps `duos_create(&duos_options_for_seed(seed)).duels` to `duel.opening.as_ref().and_then(|opening| opening.dealt.clone())`, collected into `Vec<Option<Vec<PlayerId>>>`. Assert `dealt(7) == vec![Some(vec![PlayerId::P2]), Some(vec![PlayerId::P1])]`, `dealt(3) == vec![Some(vec![PlayerId::P1]), None]` and `dealt(1) == vec![None, None]`. Seed 7 is Medium, so this also proves a 25-card handicapped deck passes `create_game`.
- `a_failure_names_its_setup_options_and_four_decks`: build `DuosSeedOutcome { seed: 7, reason: None, error: Some("planted".to_string()), heaviest: Heaviest::default(), checkpoint_paused: false, checkpoint_ms: 0 }` and call `failure_lines(std::slice::from_ref(&outcome))`. Assert it has one entry, and that the entry starts with `"seed 7: planted\n  setup: AI team medium, dealt a2, b1\n"`. With `options = duos_options_for_seed(7)`, assert the entry contains `format!("\n  options: {}\n", setup_options_json(&options))` and `"\"dealt\":[\"a2\",\"b1\"]"`, and, for each seat of `DUOS_SEATS`, `format!("\n  seed 7 {seat} deck: {}", options.decks.of(seat).join(", "))`. Then `let json = wave_json(7, 1, &[outcome]);` and assert `json["failures"][0]["seed"] == serde_json::json!(7)` and `json["failures"][0]["options"] == serde_json::to_value(&options).expect("options serialize")`.

Commands:
```
cargo test -p jackioh-tools --bin jackioh duos_fuzz      # the five new tests and the 14 existing (seeds 1–3 smoke wave, 7, 1, 1427)
cargo test -p jackioh-tools --bin jackioh replay          # replay.rs's co-op games still deal duos_decks_for_seed
cargo build --release -p jackioh-tools && target/release/jackioh fuzz --duos --seeds 200
```
If `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` is set, the binary is under that directory instead of `target/`. On `main`, the planner ran the release `fuzz --duos --seeds 200` on 4 cores: 0 failed, 58.7 s wall. The debug `duos_fuzz` tests took 12.4 s.

## Done when

- [ ] The seed rotates teams, handicaps and dealt seats (`duos_setup_for_seed`, `duos_options_for_seed`), and `play_duos_game_inner` creates every game from them.
- [ ] `the_setup_rotates_by_seed_through_every_tier_and_dealt_seats` and `two_seeds_create_different_options_and_a_seed_always_the_same` pass (rotation pinned, two seeds differ).
- [ ] `a_dealt_seat_is_dealt_in_its_own_duel_and_seat_only` passes (the `create_duel` filter is covered), and smoke seed 3 plays a dealt game through.
- [ ] `a_failure_names_its_setup_options_and_four_decks` passes (text and `--json`).
- [ ] All 14 existing `duos_fuzz` tests and the `replay` tests pass unchanged.
- [ ] `fuzz --duos --seeds 200` (release) result and wall time are recorded in the PR notes next to the baseline above.
- [ ] Header doc and README row updated.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass: rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings (no R-id is added; R184 and R433 exist), clippy, cargo tests. `cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims` should report an internal change that needs no fragment.

## Risks

- **A real engine failure surfaces.** Medium and Hard seeds, handicapped B seats and dealt decks reach paths no Duos fuzz seed reached before. If a smoke seed (1–3), seed 1427, seed 7 or seed 1 now fails, or the 200-seed wave fails, that is a finding. Do not change `DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS`, `DUOS_DEALT_SEATS` or the seed arithmetic to dodge it, and do not edit or skip a test. Report the failing seed's full `failure_report` text and the test's output, and stop. The planner could not run the rotated seeds, because its run was read-only. The planted tests change only A1's side of duel 0 (seeds 7 and 1, steps 0–4) or swap in a broken reducer. A1's deck and handicap never change, because team A is dealt first and is never handicapped, so their conditions should hold under the rotation.
- **Determinism and replay.** The setup is a pure function of the seed and opens no new random stream. The deck stream name stays `jackioh-duos-fuzz-decks-{seed}`. The fold and the checkpoint keep reading `run.options`, so replay equality checks the new options too.
- **Hidden information.** A dealt deck shows its owner less (R433). Nothing here changes a view.
- **Daily budget.** Hard seeds deal 30-card decks and a 30 pool, so their games run longer. `super.yml`'s fuzz job (90 min, not yours to edit) plays 500 Duos seeds per shard. If the 200-seed wall time more than doubles the baseline, say so in the PR notes.
- **Dead code.** Without step 3's `#[cfg(test)]`, clippy `-D warnings` fails on the unused `duos_decks_for_seed` in the binary.

## Open questions

None block the build. The builder records these decisions, each with the alternative it rejects:
- Team B is always the AI team, and team A is always `DUOS_HUMAN_TEAM` with no handicap, as `dealt_options` makes a match. Rejected: rotating which team is the AI's, which no match does.
- One dealt rotation (`[A2, B1]`) deals a team B seat, which production never does (the AI's library would be hidden from itself). It is kept so the filter's `p2` mapping is covered; the random policy reads no library. Rejected: production's A-seat subsets alone.
- Easy seeds pass `teams`/`handicaps` as `Some`, as the server does, rather than `None`. Both give the same state.
- The summary does not count seeds by setup. Rejected as beyond the acceptance criteria; the 1v1 `starts:` line is the model if a person wants it.
