## Done when

- [ ] The seed rotates teams, handicaps and dealt seats (`duos_setup_for_seed`, `duos_options_for_seed`), and `play_duos_game_inner` creates every game from them.
- [ ] `the_setup_rotates_by_seed_through_every_tier_and_dealt_seats` and `two_seeds_create_different_options_and_a_seed_always_the_same` pass (rotation pinned, two seeds differ).
- [ ] `a_dealt_seat_is_dealt_in_its_own_duel_and_seat_only` passes (the `create_duel` filter is covered), and smoke seed 3 plays a dealt game through.
- [ ] `a_failure_names_its_setup_options_and_four_decks` passes (text and `--json`).
- [ ] All 14 existing `duos_fuzz` tests and the `replay` tests pass unchanged.
- [ ] `fuzz --duos --seeds 200` (release) result and wall time are recorded in the PR notes next to the baseline above.
- [ ] Header doc and README row updated.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass: rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings (no R-id is added; R184 and R433 exist), clippy, cargo tests. `cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims` should report an internal change that needs no fragment.

## Risks

- **A real engine failure surfaces.** Medium and Hard seeds, handicapped B seats and dealt decks reach paths no Duos fuzz seed reached before. If a smoke seed (1–3), seed 1427, seed 7 or seed 1 now fails, or the 200-seed wave fails, that is a finding. Do not change `DUOS_FUZZ_TIERS`, `DUOS_DEALT_SEATS` or the seed arithmetic to dodge it, and do not edit or skip a test. Report the failing seed's full `failure_report` text and the test's output, and stop. The planner could not run the rotated seeds, because its run was read-only. The planted tests change only A1's side of duel 0 (seeds 7 and 1, steps 0–4) or swap in a broken reducer. A1's deck and handicap never change, because team A is dealt first and is never handicapped, so their conditions should hold under the rotation.
- **Determinism and replay.** The setup is a pure function of the seed and opens no new random stream. The deck stream name stays `jackioh-duos-fuzz-decks-{seed}`. The fold and the checkpoint keep reading `run.options`, so replay equality checks the new options too.
- **Hidden information.** A dealt deck shows its owner less (R433). Nothing here changes a view.
- **Daily budget.** Hard seeds deal 30-card decks and a 30 pool, so their games run longer. `super.yml`'s fuzz job (90 min, not yours to edit) plays 500 Duos seeds per shard. If the 200-seed wall time more than doubles the baseline, say so in the PR notes.
- **Dead code.** Without step 3's `#[cfg(test)]`, clippy `-D warnings` fails on the unused `duos_decks_for_seed` in the binary.

